WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:02:02.291 --> 00:02:05.250
All right, we are in Hiroshima.

00:02:05.833 --> 00:02:08.791
Right now we are at the Peace
Memorial Park.

00:02:09.166 --> 00:02:12.625
We're gonna spend our first two
days here in Hiroshima,

00:02:13.125 --> 00:02:14.500
exploring the essential spots here.

00:02:15.041 --> 00:02:17.000
And also we're gonna go to
Miyajima Island.

00:02:17.458 --> 00:02:23.125
Right now the weather is horrible, 
it's wet, it's cold, it is windy.

00:02:23.166 --> 00:02:28.375
So we decided to have an easy museum
indoors type of day.

00:02:28.541 --> 00:02:31.500
But a lot of the structures here
are also outdoors, so

00:02:31.541 --> 00:02:34.541
you can't really avoid the weather here, 
unfortunately.

00:02:34.833 --> 00:02:39.166
But we did spend a good two hours in the Peace
Memorial Museum that tells sort of

00:02:39.166 --> 00:02:42.416
the story of some of the
survivors and the

00:02:42.416 --> 00:02:44.791
tragedies that unfolded during
the bombing.

00:02:45.208 --> 00:02:49.041
Very strong imagery, probably shown a
little bit of that in this video.

00:02:49.291 --> 00:02:52.416
So if you do decide to visit, just
be prepared for that.

00:02:52.625 --> 00:02:56.083
There's some really intense images.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:16.375
I think we're heading to the castle right
now, the Hiroshima Castle.

00:03:16.583 --> 00:03:19.833
And don't know if it's gonna be any
better because of the weather, but

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:23.416
we're gonna try to make the best of it despite
the rain and everything like that.

00:03:23.416 --> 00:03:25.125
And that's how travel is
sometimes really.

00:03:25.166 --> 00:03:27.416
So let's get to it.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:37.791
All right, we just had a very, very filling
Okonomiyaki at the Okonomimura,

00:05:38.375 --> 00:05:40.916
which is the Okonomiyaki Village.

00:05:41.166 --> 00:05:47.750
Essentially four floors of small shops
that only specializes in Okonomiyaki.

00:05:48.125 --> 00:05:50.625
We decided to dine at Atom.

00:05:50.833 --> 00:05:54.458
There's also another one called Momotaro that
I heard a lot of good things about.

00:05:54.791 --> 00:05:57.916
Yeah, it's pretty decent experience,
very filling.

00:05:57.916 --> 00:06:02.250
We had to order one each, so it was a little
bit too much food than what we're

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:04.875
used to, but all good, all
good, all good.

00:06:04.875 --> 00:06:07.250
When the food is good, then it's
all good, in my opinion.

00:06:07.291 --> 00:06:12.958
So let's move on to the shopping street,
which is right next door, basically.

00:07:54.291 --> 00:07:59.250
We just arrived via the ferry
here at Miyajima Island,

00:07:59.541 --> 00:08:02.416
which is not that far from
Hiroshima City.

00:08:02.541 --> 00:08:06.666
Just an hour train ride and
ferry ride in total.

00:08:07.333 --> 00:08:09.208
And we arrived there, what's
the time right now?

00:08:09.375 --> 00:08:09.958
8 in the morning?

00:08:10.416 --> 00:08:11.291
Around 8 in the morning.

00:08:12.583 --> 00:08:14.916
And yeah, not a lot of people
here yet, but

00:08:14.916 --> 00:08:19.416
I expect it to be fully packed
by around 10.

00:08:20.208 --> 00:08:23.875
Right now we are heading towards the
shrine, and then afterwards,

00:08:24.083 --> 00:08:28.125
hopefully we could go a little trip up
a cable car, get a little view.

00:08:28.125 --> 00:08:29.500
There's a lot of clouds right now, so I'm

00:08:29.500 --> 00:08:30.916
not sure if we're going to
see anything or not.

00:08:31.083 --> 00:08:34.416
So you might be wondering why is the
camera so smooth right now?

00:08:34.625 --> 00:08:37.000
Is it some voodoo stabilization magic?

00:08:37.333 --> 00:08:41.583
It's not, it's actually a new camera
that I received from DJI.

00:08:42.083 --> 00:08:43.125
It's the Pocket 3.

00:08:43.416 --> 00:08:45.625
It's a small portable camera.

00:08:46.208 --> 00:08:49.333
I always wanted to get the
Pocket 2, but I

00:08:49.333 --> 00:08:51.625
was happy to hear when DJI
released a new one,

00:08:51.625 --> 00:08:54.916
the Pocket 3, and they were
kind enough to

00:08:54.916 --> 00:08:57.500
send this one over for me to test out for

00:08:57.500 --> 00:08:58.750
this trip in Japan.

00:08:59.416 --> 00:09:03.708
And I'm super excited to see what
I can capture with it.

00:09:03.708 --> 00:09:06.125
It's like a small compact camera, and I

00:09:06.125 --> 00:09:08.166
think it's great for like when
you're in a crowd

00:09:08.166 --> 00:09:11.500
or there's a lot of people and you
don't want to disturb anyone.

00:09:12.458 --> 00:09:14.333
So I'm thinking like restaurants,
ramen shops.

00:09:15.166 --> 00:09:18.708
We tested out at the Okonomiyaki restaurant,
and that was great.

00:09:18.708 --> 00:09:20.333
It was great to have like a
little small camera.

00:09:20.833 --> 00:09:24.083
When you're filming with a small camera,
nobody really cares.

00:09:24.625 --> 00:09:28.583
They just think you're a tourist or
it's not as scary, I guess.

00:09:29.333 --> 00:09:31.500
So yeah, looking forward
to using this.

00:09:31.916 --> 00:09:34.958
This might be my new vlogging
setup, honestly.

00:09:34.958 --> 00:09:37.375
Just how easy it is to pull
out and how less

00:09:37.375 --> 00:09:41.041
straining it is for my arms
compared to carrying

00:09:41.041 --> 00:09:42.583
the Sony FX3.

00:09:43.250 --> 00:09:47.416
And yeah, let's see how I'll like
it by the end of this trip.

00:11:43.541 --> 00:11:47.166
We are right now in Dasho-in or Daisho.

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:50.333
And it's a little bit noisy.

00:11:50.833 --> 00:11:51.958
We're still very early,

00:11:52.583 --> 00:11:54.875
but I found this little garden here

00:11:54.958 --> 00:11:59.375
where there's a lot of small Buddha
or monk statues around.

00:11:59.916 --> 00:12:01.375
A lovely little place, I would say.

00:12:45.958 --> 00:12:48.541
So we just visited Daisho-in,

00:12:48.750 --> 00:12:51.500
which is a temple here at Miyajima.

00:12:51.583 --> 00:12:55.916
It's a lovely temple, a lot of cute
little Buddha statues

00:12:56.166 --> 00:12:59.291
everywhere, and I definitely recommend
you guys to visit it.

00:13:00.041 --> 00:13:00.666
Is that Sakura?

00:13:01.083 --> 00:13:01.416
Oh, look.

00:13:01.916 --> 00:13:04.125
Our first sakura over there.

00:13:12.875 --> 00:13:17.041
We are, well, we're not that early
anymore here on Miyajima,

00:13:17.166 --> 00:13:20.750
but it has been lovely with
less people around.

00:13:20.833 --> 00:13:23.333
But of course, people are
starting to flood in

00:13:23.583 --> 00:13:24.041
to the island.

00:13:24.416 --> 00:13:26.750
I definitely recommend if you're
going to visit here,

00:13:26.750 --> 00:13:29.250
either stay overnight on the island

00:13:29.375 --> 00:13:32.125
or make the early morning journey.

00:13:32.125 --> 00:13:34.208
Maybe even the first ferry
if your hardcore.

00:14:17.208 --> 00:14:21.541
We are on top of the final stop
of the ropeway cable.

00:14:21.541 --> 00:14:25.916
So at the, I think called Shi-Shi iwa
Observatory right now.

00:14:26.291 --> 00:14:29.083
And we've got a great view over
the Miyajima Island

00:14:29.083 --> 00:14:30.791
and the surrounding small islands,

00:14:31.083 --> 00:14:32.625
and I think the mainland as well.

00:14:33.125 --> 00:14:33.958
It's snowing up here.

00:14:34.166 --> 00:14:38.875
It is not that cold, a little bit
chilly, enough for snow.

00:14:39.166 --> 00:14:42.125
The view is quite astounding,
I would say.

00:14:42.500 --> 00:14:44.000
You can just see those small islands,

00:14:44.791 --> 00:14:45.791
small boats and ships.

00:14:46.291 --> 00:14:47.750
Pretty nice, glad to be up here.

00:14:47.750 --> 00:14:50.708
We weren't able to do this on our
first trip to Hiroshima.

00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:55.041
So I'm glad that we were able
to do it this time.

00:15:40.625 --> 00:15:45.000
The lemon's okay, but the red
bean and the custard

00:15:45.750 --> 00:15:47.291
are the best in my opinion.

00:16:18.750 --> 00:16:22.958
I'm not usually an oyster kind of
guy, but it's all right.

00:16:23.666 --> 00:16:24.291
This is all right.

00:17:15.750 --> 00:17:18.750
So that was our last day
here in Hiroshima.

00:17:19.083 --> 00:17:21.000
We are heading to our next destination.

00:17:21.375 --> 00:17:23.125
We're heading to Kinosaki Onsen now

00:17:23.708 --> 00:17:26.250
for a, I guess, a more relaxing
kind of time.

00:17:26.500 --> 00:17:27.833
We're having an early train to Kinosaki.

00:17:28.333 --> 00:17:31.583
I finally feel like this trip, compared
to the last trip,

00:17:31.791 --> 00:17:36.708
we sort of had the more complete
experience of the city.

00:17:36.708 --> 00:17:38.291
There's not a lot of things
to do in Hiroshima,

00:17:38.958 --> 00:17:42.541
but there's definitely a few key
things like the peace park,

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:44.666
the museums, Miyajima Island,

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:47.375
and of course the Okonomiyaki Village.

00:17:47.791 --> 00:17:52.458
But yeah, I'm glad that we had
the chance to come back

00:17:52.583 --> 00:17:54.000
and explore properly.

00:17:54.500 --> 00:17:57.583
Now it's time to move on and
head to an onsen

00:17:57.583 --> 00:17:58.833
and try to relax a little bit

00:17:58.875 --> 00:18:04.083
before a more hectic schedule
in Kyoto and Tokyo.

00:18:04.625 --> 00:18:07.500
But anyways, see you guys
in the next one.

